If a clinician reduces an opioid then the clinician should slowly taper the opioid for a withdrawal-minimization.
If a clinician discontinues an opioid then the clinician should slowly taper the opioid for a withdrawal-minimization.
An opioid-withdrawal-symptom-and-sign-example includes an anxiety-example and includes an insomnia-example and includes an abdominal-pain-example and includes a vomiting-example and includes a diarrhea-example and includes a diaphoresis-example and includes a mydriasis-example and includes a tremor-example and includes a tachycardia-example and includes a piloerection-example.
